headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Issue Intake API

  Issues and issue comments, protected by Sanctum token authentication.

  Run **Register** (or **Login**) first: it stores the bearer token in the `token` environment variable and every other request sends it. Only the Auth requests Register and Login are public.

  Select the `local` environment (Lando, `http://issueintake.test/api/v1`).

  ## Error shape

  Every error under `/api/v1` uses the same JSON shape:

  ```json
  {"error": {"code": "validation_failed", "message": "...", "details": {"field": ["..."]}}}
  ```

  | Status | `code` | When |
  |--------|--------|------|
  | 400 | `bad_request` | Malformed JSON body |
  | 401 | `unauthenticated` | Missing, invalid or revoked bearer token |
  | 404 | `not_found` | Unknown issue id (also when commenting) or unknown route |
  | 405 | `method_not_allowed` | Unsupported method (e.g. DELETE) |
  | 422 | `validation_failed` | Invalid input or wrong login credentials; `details` lists errors per field |
  | 429 | `too_many_requests` | Register or login rate limit exceeded (6 per minute) |
  | 500 | `server_error` | Unexpected error; generic message unless `APP_DEBUG=true` |

  ## Enums

  | Field | Values |
  |-------|--------|
  | `priority` | `low`, `medium`, `high` |
  | `status` | `open`, `in_progress`, `resolved` |
  | `summary_status` (read-only) | `pending`, `ready`, `failed` |
}
